# CleverTap Flutter SDK - AI Assistant Rules

## Project Context
This is the CleverTap Flutter SDK - a wrapper around native Android and iOS SDKs.

## Critical Version Management Rules
1. ALWAYS update versions in ALL three locations:
   - pubspec.yaml (version field)
   - android/build.gradle (version field at top)
   - android/build.gradle (clevertap-android-sdk dependency)

2. CHANGELOG.md format is STRICT and MUST be preserved:
   - New entries at the TOP
   - Format: "Version X.X.X *(DD Month YYYY)*"
   - Platform sections: [Android Platform], [iOS Platform], [Web Platform]
   - Link to native SDK changelogs

3. Flutter SDK version is INDEPENDENT from native SDK versions
   - Example: Flutter v3.6.0 can use Android SDK v7.6.0
   - Both need to be documented separately

## File Modification Guidelines
- Use edit_file() for precise changes, not full rewrites
- Always read files before modifying to understand structure
- Validate changes by reading back after editing
- Show diffs to user for review

## When Adding New APIs
- Must implement in BOTH Android and iOS
- Update lib/clevertap_plugin.dart
- Update doc/Usage.md with examples
- Add to CHANGELOG.md under "API changes"

## Commit Message Format
Use conventional commits:
- feat(platform): description
- fix(platform): description
- chore: description
- docs: description

## Automation
- Use claude_tasks/*.md for repeatable workflows
- Scripts in root: ct-update.sh, ct-natural.sh
- Always validate before and after changes

## Testing Requirements
- Test on both Android and iOS
- Run example app after changes
- Verify version consistency across files

## Documentation
See Claude.md for comprehensive project documentation
